@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam defaultFontColor #000000
hide circle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classBorderColor #000000
skinparam classFontColor #000000
skinparam stereotypeFontColor #000000
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #000000
skinparam noteFontSize 14
skinparam titleFontSize 24
skinparam titleFontColor #000000
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam packageBorderColor #000000
hide empty members
title Observer - order status notifications
left to right direction
class OrderProgress <<subject>> {
  - observers : Set<OrderObserver>
  - status : OrderStatus
  + subscribe(observer)
  + unsubscribe(observer)
  + announce()
  + advance()
  - notifyObservers()
}
interface OrderObserver <<observer>> {
  + onStatusChanged(change) : OrderNotification
}
class CustomerObserver <<concrete observer>>
class KitchenObserver <<concrete observer>>
class OperationsDashboardObserver <<concrete observer>> {
  - itemQuantity : int
}
class StatusChange <<record>> {
  + orderId() : UUID
  + status() : OrderStatus
  + occurredAt() : Instant
}
class OrderNotification <<record>> {
  + status() : OrderStatus
  + message() : String
  + audience() : String
}
OrderProgress "1" o--> "0..*" OrderObserver : notifies
OrderObserver <|.. CustomerObserver
OrderObserver <|.. KitchenObserver
OrderObserver <|.. OperationsDashboardObserver
OrderProgress ..> StatusChange : publishes
OrderObserver ..> StatusChange : receives
OrderObserver ..> OrderNotification : returns
OrderProgress --> OrderNotification : stores event history
note bottom of OrderProgress
PLACED → PREPARING → READY → COMPLETED
Invalid transitions fail before notification.
Customer/kitchen events and operations events
are projected into the same session-owned order view.
end note
@enduml
